WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Your career starts the day you walk out of here. Let's make sure you're ready.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Professional conduct and customer service. Arrive on time. Wear a clean uniform.
Put on shoe covers before entering a home. Explain what you are doing and why.
Present options with costs and let the customer decide. Clean up your work area

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Technical skills get you hired. Professional
conduct keeps you employed and builds your reputation.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: First impressions matter — clean uniform, on time. And —
Explain in plain language

00:02:24.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

